Title: The Night Ferry
Credit: Sample scene
Author: The Cold Open contributors
Draft date: November 2026

INT. FERRY TERMINAL - NIGHT

Rain sheets down the long windows. A departures board clicks through cancelled crossings, one by one.

NORA (40s, raincoat buttoned wrong) sits alone on a bench with a cardboard box on her knees. Something inside it shifts.

The door bangs open. ELI (30s, soaked, out of breath) shakes off an umbrella that has given up.

ELI
They said the last boat already left.

NORA
They say a lot of things.

ELI
Is that it?

He nods at the box. Nora holds it a little tighter.

NORA
You were supposed to be here at nine.

ELI
I was here at nine. I was at the other terminal at nine.

NORA
There's only one terminal.

ELI
(beat)
There's two now. They built one.

A long horn sounds from the dark water. Both of them turn.

Out past the pier, the lights of a small ferry swing toward the dock.

NORA
That's not on the board.

ELI
Nothing good ever is.

He offers his hand for the box. She doesn't give it to him. She stands instead.

NORA
We go together, or we don't go.

They walk out into the rain.

EXT. FERRY DOCK - CONTINUOUS

The ferry bumps against the pilings. A DECKHAND in a yellow slicker lowers the ramp and looks them over.

DECKHAND
Two?

NORA
Three.

The box shifts again. The deckhand decides not to ask.

CUT TO:
